  "name": "Example: Separating a Square Root Into a Product of Two Square Roots",
  "problem": "Simplify $\\sqrt{12}.$",
  "worked_solution": "Note that $12=4 \\cdot 3,$ where $4$ is a perfect square. So, applying the product rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{12} =\\sqrt{4 \\cdot 3}= \\sqrt{4} \\cdot \\sqrt{3} = 2\\sqrt{3}.\n$$",
